{#
  HubSpot tracking code: marketing analytics for HubSpot portal 149809135
  (EU data centre, "eu1").

  HubSpot's install instruction is one static tag on every page, directly
  before </body>:

    <script type="text/javascript" id="hs-script-loader" async defer
            src="//js-eu1.hs-scripts.com/149809135.js"></script>

  This partial sits at that position (last include in layouts/base.njk, so
  on every page) and creates exactly that element, but only after consent.

  CONSENT-GATED, same rule and same switch as leadfeeder.njk. The tracking
  code writes visitor identifiers to the device (__hstc and hubspotutk for
  six months, __hssc for 30 minutes, __hssrc for the session) and sends them
  to HubSpot with every hit. That is storage/access on the visitor's terminal
  equipment for a non-essential purpose, so § 25(1) TDDDG requires prior
  consent. The loader is therefore requested only once 'vornac_consent_v1'
  is "granted": on a stored choice at page load, or the moment the visitor
  clicks "Accept all" in consent-banner.njk. Without consent no request
  goes to HubSpot at all.

  Consent hand-over to HubSpot (cookie banner API on developers.hubspot.com):
    window.disableHubSpotCookieBanner = true
        Our modal is the only consent UI. HubSpot's own banner must never
        stack on top of it, whatever is configured in the portal. HubSpot
        requires the flag to be set before its banner code loads.
    _hsp.push(['setHubSpotConsent', {...}])
        Tells the tracking code that consent exists. HubSpot does not
        persist this value itself, so it is re-sent on every pageview from
        the stored choice.
  Only the "analytics" category is released. "functionality" (HubSpot chat)
  and "advertisement" (ad pixels HubSpot can install through this loader)
  stay false: neither is in use and neither is described in the privacy
  policy. Releasing one means changing it here and on /legal together.

  Withdrawal ("Essential only" after an earlier "Accept all"): consent is
  re-sent as false, HubSpot is asked to drop its cookies
  (revokeCookieConsent), and the cookies are deleted here as well, so the
  result does not depend on HubSpot's code. The same sweep runs on every
  pageview without a stored "granted".

  The __vornacLangRedirect check mirrors head-analytics.njk, leadfeeder.njk
  and google-tag.njk. Nothing sets that flag since the automatic language
  redirect was removed (see lang-redirect.njk); the check stays so that all
  trackers behave alike should a redirect ever come back.

  Good to know when checking the installation: the tag is not in the page
  source and HubSpot's "Validate your tracking code" tool can report a
  failure, exactly as with a tag manager, because the tag only exists in the
  DOM after consent. To verify, accept cookies and look for 149809135.js and
  __ptq.gif in the network tab.
#}
<script>
(function () {
    var KEY = 'vornac_consent_v1';
    var SRC = {{ site.analytics.hubspotScript | dump | safe }};
    var loaded = false;

    // Everything the tracking code keeps first-party: visitor and session
    // cookies (__hstc, __hssc, __hssrc, hubspotutk), HubSpot's own
    // consent-state cookies (__hs_*), chat cookies, and its web storage
    // entries.
    var COOKIES = /^(__hs|hubspotutk$|messagesUtk$|hs-messages-)/;
    var STORAGE = /^(__hs|__hmpl$|hublytics_events_)/;

    function sendConsent(granted) {
        var hsp = window._hsp = window._hsp || [];
        hsp.push(['setHubSpotConsent', {
            analytics: granted,
            advertisement: false,
            functionality: false
        }]);
    }

    function load() {
        window.disableHubSpotCookieBanner = true;
        sendConsent(true);
        if (loaded) return;
        loaded = true;
        // HubSpot's embed tag, attribute for attribute.
        var s = document.createElement('script');
        s.type = 'text/javascript';
        s.id = 'hs-script-loader';
        s.async = true;
        s.defer = true;
        s.src = SRC;
        document.body.appendChild(s);
    }

    function sweep() {
        var root = location.hostname.replace(/^www\./, '');
        var domains = ['', '; domain=' + root, '; domain=.' + root];
        document.cookie.split(';').forEach(function (pair) {
            var name = pair.split('=')[0].trim();
            if (!COOKIES.test(name)) return;
            domains.forEach(function (d) {
                document.cookie = name + '=; Max-Age=0; path=/' + d;
            });
        });
        ['localStorage', 'sessionStorage'].forEach(function (area) {
            try {
                var store = window[area];
                Object.keys(store).forEach(function (name) {
                    if (STORAGE.test(name)) store.removeItem(name);
                });
            } catch (e) {}
        });
    }

    function purge() {
        if (loaded) {
            // HubSpot is on the page: withdraw consent there too, then sweep
            // a second time in case its code writes once more on the way out.
            sendConsent(false);
            window._hsp.push(['revokeCookieConsent']);
            setTimeout(sweep, 1000);
        }
        sweep();
    }

    // consent-banner.njk drives these when the visitor makes or changes a choice.
    window.__vornacHubspot = { load: load, purge: purge };

    var stored = null;
    try { stored = localStorage.getItem(KEY); } catch (e) {}

    if (stored !== 'granted') {
        purge();
        return;
    }
    if (window.__vornacLangRedirect) return;
    load();
})();
</script>
